                <pb facs="0442" n="932" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p2/pg932"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/8–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-14T14:00:00+01:00">August 14, 1948—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3689. For Brown (State) and Draper (Army) from Marbury for Stinebower and Leddy.
                    British will cooperate in preparation of multi-lateral agreement on Germany.
                    Douglas feels that it would be unwise to insist on British participation in
                    drafting similar agreement on Japan but has strongly urged Foreign Office to
                    instruct delegation at Geneva to begin informal exploratory talks on a
                    multilateral basis. From latest indications it seems probable that Foreign
                    Office will accept Douglas’ suggestion but concurrence of President BOT must
                    first be obtained early next week. Caffery not available until Monday. Leddy
                    proceeding direct to Geneva. Marbury will see Caffery on Monday and then proceed
                    Geneva. Upon his arrival US Delegation will ask that this matter be brought up
                    for immediate consideration and reference to sub-committee to prepare final
                    draft of multilateral agreement on Germany and to consider suggestions for
                    tentative draft on Japan.</p>
                <pb facs="0443" n="933" xml:id="pg933"/>
                <p>Sent Department 3689; repeated Geneva 68. [Marbury (for Stinebower) and
                    Leddy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
